#
# 2026-09-22 (this entry): reviewed 4a9b8f7 (v0.137, 2026-09-21), diffing from
# c830486 (2026-09-17), which is the oldest state that happened to be on disk
# rather than a previously reviewed point. 16 commits, 88 files. Five files of
# shared Java changed and every edit was COMMENT-ONLY. Taken: their correction
# to the Rogers Kbf note, which called an aft CP shift "a more conservative
# static margin" when aft RAISES the displayed margin (see the FinSetCalc patch
# and CHANGELOG). Skipped, as not applicable: their RK4SimulationStepper
# parallel-stage nozzle correction - we do not carry that patch, have no
# pressure-thrust half for our drag half to disagree with, and expose
# nozzleExitDiameter in no UI; and their turbulence-seed documentation fix,
# whose analogue here ("auto" quietly meaning the constant 42) was already
# found and fixed in web/src/services/simulations.ts.
#
# 2026-09-27: reviewed 76d8035 (v0.142, 2026-09-24), diffing from 4a9b8f7, the
# previous reviewed point. 439 commits and 440 files, of which 17 files and 11
# commits are under engine-java. Their five new or changed kernel patches split
# three ways.
#
# TAKEN: the self-intersecting freeform outline. `FreeformFinSet.setPoints`
# refuses a crossing outline by rolling it back and logging, which through a
# bridge means flying the CONSTRUCTOR'S DEFAULT FIN - measured here at length
# 0.325 m / CP 0.2588 m against the drawn outline's 0.300 m / 0.2454 m, with no
# error anywhere. Their fix and ours are the same shape (a recorded refusal the
# bridge reads and throws on, a deliberate divergence from desktop's silent
# substitution); the half of their entry about a TeaVM `%g` crash does not apply,
# because those two log lines were rebuilt with string concatenation here when
# the file was first patched for `Geo2D`. See patches/LEDGER.md, "A refused fin
# outline is no longer flown as the default fin".
#
# NOT APPLICABLE: their `BarrowmanCalculator` aft-base nozzle credit and the
# matching `RK4SimulationStepper` per-stage-instance pressure thrust. Both halves
# belong to a patch pair we do not carry - this engine rides upstream's own
# per-motor `MotorConfiguration.nozzleExitDiameter` and
# `getThrustingNozzleExitArea`, unpatched - so there is nothing here for either
# correction to land on. Their re-carve of the `FinSetCalc` Kbf comment is the
# correction this file's 2026-09-22 entry already took.
#
# SKIPPED, A DECISION NOT A GAP: `MassCalculation` + `RingComponent`, an off-axis
# motor mount and its tube carrying their parallel-axis ROLL inertia. The defect
# is real and is upstream 24.12's, byte for byte: a single inner tube placed off
# the centerline (the everyday split cluster) contributes no transport term, and
# a cluster's tubes miss their spread about the mean. Taking it would break the
# claim this engine is built on - bit-identical to upstream - for an inertia term
# no view here reports as its own number, so it is recorded as an inherited
# inaccuracy instead. Revisit if roll rate is ever published as a result.
#
# NOT TAKEN: their seeded `addWindLevel` (`MultiLevelPinkNoiseWindModel`).
# Applicable, and not done in this pass. This bridge builds the multi-level
# model through upstream's unseeded overload, so a flight with turbulent wind
# levels is not reproducible run to run; the single-level path here has been
# seeded from `randomSeed` since it was written.
